WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.984 --> 00:00:03.715
- [Host] La Scarzuola began
as a Franciscan monastery,

00:00:03.715 --> 00:00:07.382
but today, it's an
architectural wonderland.

00:00:10.092 --> 00:00:12.407
In the 1950s, an architect
named Tomaso Buzzi

00:00:12.407 --> 00:00:14.786
purchased La Scarzuola in Terni, Italy,

00:00:14.786 --> 00:00:18.231
with the intention of turning
it into his own ideal city.

00:00:18.231 --> 00:00:20.371
Each work is carefully
thought out and built

00:00:20.371 --> 00:00:22.790
to represent an inner thought of Tomaso.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:27.106
He considered this his
autobiography in stone.

00:00:27.106 --> 00:00:29.196
La Scarzuola was formed by seven theaters

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:31.272
representing Tomaso's
notion that the ideal life

00:00:31.272 --> 00:00:33.363
is symbolically theatrical.

00:00:33.363 --> 00:00:36.006
Influenced by Dali and
Escher, his style is a blend

00:00:36.006 --> 00:00:38.843
of surrealistic architecture,
and neo mannerist elements

00:00:38.843 --> 00:00:40.590
which can be felt in the general unbalance

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.115
and disproportionate feel of the place.

00:00:43.115 --> 00:00:44.773
These elements are meant
to reflect Tomaso's

00:00:44.773 --> 00:00:47.580
passionate belief that
life is both mysterious

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.830
and perplexing.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.060
After Tomaso passed in 1981,

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.181
his nephew continued
to work on La Scarzuola

00:00:54.181 --> 00:00:55.734
to complete his uncle's vision,

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:59.151
allowing Tomaso's ideal city to live on.

